statement:
Let $n$ be a positive integer.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] Prove that there exists a set $S$ of $6n$ pairwise different positive integers such that the least common multiple of any two elements of $S$ is no larger than $32n^2$.
\item[(b)] Prove that every set $T$ of $6n$ pairwise different positive integers contains two elements whose least common multiple is larger than $9n^2$.
\end{enumerate}
